{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Bound the post-kill `proc.communicate()` with a timeout so a child that does not die to SIGKILL cannot hang run_observability indefinitely.","criteria":["error-handling","correctness"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["_observability_harness.py:113-114: `_kill_group(proc.pid)` then `proc.communicate()` with no timeout","The docstring motivation (commit message) is that stock-macOS runs waited on the real daemon unbounded; a D-state child blocks the uncapped reap the same way"],"finding":"On the timeout/interrupt path, after killing the process group with SIGKILL, run_observability calls proc.communicate() with no timeout. If any process in the group fails to terminate promptly (e.g. a child in uninterruptible D-state waiting on the host Docker daemon or a stuck mount), this second communicate() blocks indefinitely, defeating the very timeout bound the harness exists to enforce.","id":"0","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/scripts/_observability_harness.py:113","norm_id":"n9ed19155e7c0d56a","priority":0.1929,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"Pass a finite timeout to the reaping communicate() (e.g. proc.communicate(timeout=5)) and let a secondary TimeoutExpired surface rather than block forever.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the direct-run AST scan (or document the limitation) so a subprocess call whose argv is an intermediate variable holding str(SCRIPT) is still detected.","criteria":["error-handling","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["test_observability_harness_isolation.py:155-170: hits only when `any(_names_script(item, ...) for item in _argv_items(node.args[0]))`, and _argv_items only unpacks ast.List/ast.Tuple else returns [argv]","_names_script returns True only for an ast.Name whose id is in script_names or str(Name); a variable holding the argv list is an ast.Name bound to a List, which is not in script_names","The anti-vacuity test only exercises the inline-list form (test_sample.py:4), so the aliased-argv gap is uncovered"],"finding":"The AST guard _direct_script_runs only flags a subprocess call whose FIRST argument is a literal list/tuple (or str()) that textually contains the SCRIPT name. A test that binds the argv to a variable first (cmd = [\"bash\", str(SCRIPT)]; subprocess.run(cmd, ...)) runs the script directly yet is invisible to the scan, so the isolation guarantee fails open for that pattern.","id":"1","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/scripts/test_observability_harness_isolation.py:168","norm_id":"nfdf04e9b09738ad4","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace the verbatim source-text grep in test_the_instance_id_cache_follows_the_redirected_region_cache with a behavioral check (e.g. run the script with a redirected REGION_CACHE and assert the written INSTANCE_ID_CACHE lands under tmp_path), keeping the source-literal assertion only if it is relaxed to not pin the internal variable name.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/scripts/test_observability_harness_isolation.py:71: `assert 'INSTANCE_ID_CACHE=\"${INSTANCE_ID_CACHE:-${REGION_CACHE_DIR}/' in SCRIPT.read_text()`","The grepped token `REGION_CACHE_DIR` is an internal shell variable consumed only by bash (infra/scripts/observability.sh:71-73), not by any non-human parser/registry, so it is source-grepping an implementation detail rather than a structural contract.","The adjacent assertions at lines 76-77 (`Path(env['INSTANCE_ID_CACHE']).parent == Path(env['REGION_CACHE']).parent` and `startswith(str(tmp_path))`) already verify the behaviorally-relevant outcome of observability_env without depending on the exact source text."],"finding":"test_the_instance_id_cache_follows_the_redirected_region_cache asserts a verbatim fragment of observability.sh's source text ('INSTANCE_ID_CACHE=\"${INSTANCE_ID_CACHE:-${REGION_CACHE_DIR}/') rather than an observable behavior. This is a source-grep over the script under test coupled to the internal variable name REGION_CACHE_DIR; a behavior-preserving rename of that variable (while still placing instance-id beside the region cache) would break the test even though the harness's explicit INSTANCE_ID_CACHE override keeps isolation intact.","id":"2","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/scripts/test_observability_harness_isolation.py:71","norm_id":"nb6b85960da66c115","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["observability.sh is refactored to rename REGION_CACHE_DIR or restructure the derivation while still placing probe-instance-id beside the region cache."],"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_